('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha is Withania somnifera, an evergreen shrub found in parts of India, Africa and the Middle East.', 'Meet ashwagandha (Withania somnifera), an evergreen shrub with deep roots in traditional wellness.', 'Meet ashwagandha (Withania somnifera), an evergreen shrub with deep roots in traditional wellness.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A1 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS Ashwagandha fact sheet; NCCIH Ashwagandha (2023)', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'The Sanskrit name ashwagandha means roughly ''smell of horse'', after the root''s earthy odor.', 'Ashwagandha means ''smell of a horse'' in Sanskrit, a nod to its earthy root.', 'Ashwagandha means ''smell of a horse'' in Sanskrit, a nod to its earthy root.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A2 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Ambiye et al., Evid Based Complement Alternat Med 2013', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'The species name somnifera comes from the Latin for ''sleep-inducing''.', 'Somnifera comes from the Latin for sleep bringing. Even its name hints at evening calm.', 'Somnifera comes from the Latin for sleep bringing. Even its name hints at evening calm.', 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A3 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Langade et al., J Ethnopharmacol 2021', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha root has been used in Ayurvedic and Unani medicine as an adaptogen, traditionally used to help the body adapt to everyday stressors.', 'In Ayurveda, ashwagandha root is an adaptogen: traditionally used to help the body adapt to everyday stress.', 'In Ayurveda, ashwagandha root is an adaptogen: traditionally used to help the body adapt to everyday stress.', 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A4 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS (citing Panossian 2021); Gerontakos, Yale J Biol Med 2020', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha is nicknamed ''Indian ginseng'' but is not in the ginseng family.', 'Nicknamed ''Indian ginseng'', ashwagandha isn''t actually related to ginseng. It''s its own plant.', 'Nicknamed ''Indian ginseng'', ashwagandha isn''t actually related to ginseng. It''s its own plant.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha', 'research library 2026-11 · A5 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; NCCIH', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha root and leaf have different chemical makeups; most commercial supplements and most research use root extract.', 'Root and leaf aren''t the same. Ashwagandha root and leaf have different chemistry, and most research uses the root.', 'Root and leaf aren''t the same. Ashwagandha root and leaf have different chemistry, and most research uses the root.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A6 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS (citing India Ministry of AYUSH expert report 2024)', 'product_match', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha''s main compounds are steroidal lactones called withanolides, plus alkaloids.', 'Withanolides are the natural compounds ashwagandha root is best known for.', 'Withanolides are the natural compounds ashwagandha root is best known for.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A7 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Holvoet, Nutrients 2022', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'KSM-66 is a full-spectrum, root-only ashwagandha extract standardized to at least 5% withanolides, used in multiple published human trials (Chandrasekhar 2012, Ambiye 2013, Wankhede 2015, Langade 2021).', 'Our ashwagandha is KSM-66, a root-only extract standardized to at least 5% withanolides and used in multiple published human trials.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3863556/', 'research library 2026-11 · A8 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Ambiye et al. 2013 (PMC3863556); ClinicalTrials.gov NCT07890935', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'In Ayurveda, ashwagandha root is traditionally regarded as a rasayana, a rejuvenating tonic.', 'For thousands of years, Ayurveda has prized ashwagandha root as a daily rejuvenating tonic.', 'For thousands of years, Ayurveda has prized ashwagandha root as a daily rejuvenating tonic.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3863556/', 'research library 2026-11 · A9 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'Ambiye 2013; BJPsych Open 2025', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ashwagandha trials use many different extracts (root only, root and leaf, sustained release) at 240 to 1,250 mg a day, so results from one extract don''t automatically apply to another.', 'Not all ashwagandha is equal: studies differ by plant part, extract and dose. That''s why we use a root-only, standardized extract.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · A10 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Speers et al., Curr Neuropharmacol 2021', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Chandrasekhar 2012: 64 chronically stressed adults took 600 mg/day KSM-66 root extract for 60 days; serum cortisol fell 27.9% and perceived stress dropped vs placebo.', 'In a 60-day double-blind study of 64 stressed adults, 600 mg/day KSM-66 root extract was linked with lower perceived stress and serum cortisol vs placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23439798/', 'research library 2026-11 · B1 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Chandrasekhar et al., Indian J Psychol Med 2012;34:255-62, PMID 23439798', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Lopresti and Smith 2021 systematic review of 7 RCTs (491 adults, 6 to 8 weeks): ashwagandha reduced stress scores, sleeplessness, fatigue and serum cortisol vs placebo; 500 to 600 mg/day looked better than lower doses.', 'A 2021 review of 7 trials found ashwagandha extracts were linked with lower stress scores and cortisol vs placebo, especially at 500 to 600 mg a day.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B2 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Lopresti & Smith, J Herbal Med 2021;28:100434', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Akhgarjand 2022 meta-analysis of 12 RCTs (1,002 participants): lower stress and anxiety scores; best stress effect at 300 to 600 mg/day; certainty of evidence rated low.', 'A 2022 meta-analysis of 12 trials linked ashwagandha with lower perceived stress; researchers called the evidence promising but low certainty.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/ptr.7598', 'research library 2026-11 · B3 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Akhgarjand et al., Phytother Res 2022;36:4115-24', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'A 2025 meta-analysis of RCTs in stressed adults found ashwagandha lowered perceived stress and cortisol vs placebo at 8 weeks.', 'A 2025 meta-analysis reported lower stress scores and cortisol after 8 weeks of ashwagandha vs placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12242034/', 'research library 2026-11 · B4 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'BJPsych Open 2025, DOI 10.1192/bjo.2025.10136', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Gopukumar 2021: 130 stressed adults took a sustained-release root extract for 90 days; stress, sleep quality and self-rated memory and focus improved and serum cortisol fell vs placebo.', 'In a 90-day trial, a root extract was linked with better self-rated focus, memory and sleep quality vs placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34858513/', 'research library 2026-11 · B6 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Gopukumar et al., Evid Based Complement Alternat Med 2021, PMID 34858513', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Smith 2023: 120 adults with low energy took a root extract (Witholytin) for 12 weeks; fatigue fell but perceived stress did not change.', 'A 12-week trial found a root extract eased self-rated fatigue, though stress scores didn''t change.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B8 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Smith et al., J Psychopharmacol 2023;37:1091-104', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Baker 2022 (University of Colorado): students taking a root extract for 30 days described calm, energy, clearer thinking and stress that felt more manageable.', 'College students in a 30-day US study described stress as more manageable on ashwagandha root extract.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B9 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Baker et al., J Med Food 2022;25:1095; NCT05430685', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Langade 2021: 80 adults took KSM-66 600 mg/day for 8 weeks; sleep quality and time to fall asleep improved (actigraphy), including in healthy sleepers.', 'In an 8-week KSM-66 trial, healthy adults reported better sleep quality vs placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B10 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Langade et al., J Ethnopharmacol 2021;264:113276', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Cheah 2021 meta-analysis of 5 RCTs (372 adults): a small but significant sleep benefit, larger at 600 mg/day and with 8+ weeks of use.', 'Pooled trials suggest ashwagandha''s sleep support is modest and builds over about 8 weeks at 600 mg a day.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B11 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Cheah et al., PLoS One 2021;16:e0257843', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'usage', 'In ashwagandha trials, sleep and stress benefits appeared after weeks (6 to 12) of daily use, not overnight.', 'Ashwagandha isn''t a quick fix. In studies, benefits appeared with daily use over several weeks.', 'Ashwagandha isn''t a quick fix. In studies, benefits appeared with daily use over several weeks.', 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · B12 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Cheah 2021', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Choudhary 2017 studied ashwagandha root extract for body-weight management and stress-related eating in chronically stressed adults (double-blind, placebo-controlled).', 'Researchers have studied ashwagandha root for stress-related eating habits.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27055824/', 'research library 2026-11 · B16 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Choudhary et al. 2017, PMID 27055824', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Wankhede 2015: 57 young men took KSM-66 600 mg/day for 8 weeks of resistance training; bench-press gain 46.0 kg vs 26.4 kg on placebo, better recovery marker (creatine kinase) and more body fat lost (3.5% vs 1.5%).', 'In an 8-week training study, men taking KSM-66 root extract gained more strength and showed better recovery markers than placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1186/s12970-015-0104-9', 'research library 2026-11 · B17 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Wankhede et al., J Int Soc Sports Nutr 2015;12:43', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Choudhary 2015: healthy athletic adults took KSM-66 600 mg/day for 8 weeks; VO2 max rose significantly vs placebo.', 'In athletes, 8 weeks of KSM-66 was linked with better VO2 max vs placebo.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/26730141/', 'research library 2026-11 · B19 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Choudhary et al., Ayu 2015;36:63-68, PMID 26730141', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'NCCIH: some ashwagandha preparations may help with stress and sleep, but evidence on athletic performance and cognitive function is not yet enough.', 'Research on ashwagandha is promising but still growing; the NIH says more large studies are needed.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha', 'research library 2026-11 · B25 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'NCCIH Ashwagandha; NIH ODS', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'A 12-month observational study of KSM-66 600 mg/day in healthy adults found no harmful changes in liver, kidney or thyroid markers.', 'A 12-month study of KSM-66 reported no adverse changes in liver, kidney or thyroid markers in healthy adults. Talk with your healthcare provider about long-term use.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ptr.70096', 'research library 2026-11 · B26 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Phytother Res 2025, DOI 10.1002/ptr.70096', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'NCCIH and NIH ODS safety statements cover adults only; there is no official pediatric dosing.', 'For adults 18 and over.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha', 'research library 2026-11 · C3 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'NCCIH; NIH ODS', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Ashwagandha has been well tolerated for up to about 3 months in trials; mild effects can include stomach upset, loose stools, nausea or drowsiness; long-term safety is not established.', 'Most studies ran up to 3 months. Talk with your healthcare provider about longer use.', 'Most studies ran up to 3 months. Talk with your healthcare provider about longer use.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · C4 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; NCCIH', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Ashwagandha may affect thyroid function and may interact with thyroid medication.', 'If you take thyroid medication, check with your doctor before ashwagandha.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · C5 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS; Sharma 2018', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Rare cases of liver injury have been reported with ashwagandha, all improving after stopping.', 'Rarely, liver issues have been reported. Stop and see a doctor if you notice yellowing skin or dark urine.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · C6 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'Björnsson, Liver Int 2020; NIH LiverTox', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Ashwagandha may interact with diabetes and blood-pressure medicines, immunosuppressants, sedatives and thyroid hormone.', 'On medication? Ask your pharmacist before adding ashwagandha.', 'On medication? Ask your pharmacist before adding ashwagandha.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · C7 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NIH ODS', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Ashwagandha should be avoided during pregnancy and breastfeeding.', 'Not for use during pregnancy or breastfeeding.', 'Not for use during pregnancy or breastfeeding.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha', 'research library 2026-11 · C8 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NCCIH; NIH ODS', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'NCCIH advises against ashwagandha before surgery and urges caution with thyroid or autoimmune conditions.', 'Have surgery coming up or an autoimmune condition? Pause and check with your doctor.', 'Have surgery coming up or an autoimmune condition? Pause and check with your doctor.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/ashwagandha', 'research library 2026-11 · C9 · SS', 'ashwagandha', 'NCCIH 2023', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Ashwagandha belongs to the nightshade family (Solanaceae).', 'Ashwagandha is in the nightshade family (Solanaceae), worth knowing if you avoid nightshades.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · C12 · CO', 'ashwagandha', 'W. somnifera plant family: Solanaceae (NIH ODS)', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Shilajit is a blackish-brown resin that seeps from rock in the Himalayan and other mountain ranges, formed over centuries from decomposed plant matter.', 'Shilajit is a mineral-rich resin that seeps from mountain rock, formed over centuries from ancient plant matter.', 'Shilajit is a mineral-rich resin that seeps from mountain rock, formed over centuries from ancient plant matter.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6364418/', 'research library 2026-11 · D1 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Yadav, Cureus 2026 (PMC12848467); Keller, JISSN 2019 (PMC6364418)', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Ayurveda has used shilajit for centuries as a rasayana, a rejuvenating tonic.', 'In Ayurveda, shilajit is a rasayana, a traditional rejuvenating tonic.', 'In Ayurveda, shilajit is a rasayana, a traditional rejuvenating tonic.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · D2 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Cureus 2026; Pandit, Andrologia 2016', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Shilajit is mostly humic substances; fulvic acid is its best-studied fraction.', 'Shilajit is rich in fulvic acid, a natural compound formed as plants slowly break down.', 'Shilajit is rich in fulvic acid, a natural compound formed as plants slowly break down.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · D3 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Shilajit composition review 2023; Cureus 2026', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Shilajit contains dibenzo-alpha-pyrones (DBPs), amino acids, fatty acids and phenolics; DBPs and fulvic acid are considered its key actives.', 'Fulvic acid and dibenzo-alpha-pyrones are two of shilajit''s signature natural compounds.', 'Fulvic acid and dibenzo-alpha-pyrones are two of shilajit''s signature natural compounds.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ptr.5018', 'research library 2026-11 · D4 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Stohs, Phytother Res 2014;28:475-9', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Shilajit naturally contains a broad spectrum of trace minerals, dominated by calcium, potassium and magnesium.', 'Shilajit naturally carries a broad spectrum of trace minerals.', 'Shilajit naturally carries a broad spectrum of trace minerals.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · D5 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Cureus 2026; shilajit composition review', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'quality', 'Raw shilajit''s mineral matrix can include unwanted trace elements such as arsenic and varies by where it is mined.', 'Raw shilajit can carry unwanted metals from the rock. That''s why purification and testing matter.', 'Raw shilajit can carry unwanted metals from the rock. That''s why purification and testing matter.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ptr.5018', 'research library 2026-11 · D6 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Shilajit composition review 2023; Stohs 2014', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'quality', 'The TruBlk resin in its published study was made in a GMP facility by solvent-free water extraction, standardized to at least 60% fulvic acids and tested for heavy metals, microbes, pesticides, aflatoxins and PAHs.', 'The TruBlk resin used in published research is water extracted, standardized to at least 60% fulvic acids and tested for heavy metals.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · D7 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Yadav et al., Cureus 2026;18:e102372, PMID 41613504', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'TruBlk pilot: 25 healthy active men took 500 mg/day for 28 days (open label, no placebo); leg-press 1RM rose 12.9%, endurance 12.3%, fatigue score fell 32.4%.', 'In a 28-day open-label pilot (no placebo group), men taking TruBlk shilajit resin 500 mg a day reported less fatigue and gained strength; the authors work with the ingredient maker.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · E1 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Yadav et al., Cureus 2026, PMID 41613504', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'In the 28-day TruBlk pilot, no serious adverse events were reported and liver, kidney and blood labs stayed in the normal range.', 'No serious side effects were reported and lab safety markers stayed in normal range over 28 days.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12848467/', 'research library 2026-11 · E2 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Yadav et al., Cureus 2026', 'product_match', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Keller 2019: 63 active men took purified shilajit 250 or 500 mg/day for 8 weeks; at 500 mg/day, strength held up better after a fatiguing exercise protocol vs placebo.', 'In an 8-week placebo-controlled study, purified shilajit 500 mg a day helped men keep more strength after fatiguing exercise.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC6364418/', 'research library 2026-11 · E4 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Keller et al., J Int Soc Sports Nutr 2019 (PMC6364418)', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Neltner 2024: 8 weeks of 500 or 1,000 mg/day purified shilajit raised a blood marker of type 1 collagen synthesis vs placebo.', 'A placebo-controlled study linked purified shilajit with higher blood markers of new collagen production.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ijrpr.com/uploads/V6ISSUE12/IJRPR57032.pdf', 'research library 2026-11 · E5 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Neltner et al. 2024 (RCT)', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Das 2019: middle-aged women took purified shilajit 250 mg twice daily for 14 weeks; skin microcirculation improved, with no adverse skin effects.', 'A 14-week study linked purified shilajit with improved skin microcirculation in women.', null, 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://www.researchgate.net/publication/333628674', 'research library 2026-11 · E6 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Das et al., J Am Coll Nutr 2019; NCT02762032', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
