('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'research', 'Stohs 2014 review: relatively few well-controlled human studies exist on shilajit; more are needed.', 'Research on shilajit is growing, but scientists agree more large human studies are needed.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ptr.5018', 'research library 2026-11 · E11 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Stohs, Phytother Res 2014, PMID 23733436', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Shilajit''s safety record in studies applies to purified, standardized material.', 'Choose shilajit that''s purified and lab tested for heavy metals.', 'Choose shilajit that''s purified and lab tested for heavy metals.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/ptr.5018', 'research library 2026-11 · F1 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Stohs 2014; Cureus 2026', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Raw or poorly processed shilajit can contain heavy metals, mycotoxins and microbes.', 'Raw isn''t better. Unpurified shilajit can carry contaminants. Purification makes the difference.', 'Raw isn''t better. Unpurified shilajit can carry contaminants. Purification makes the difference.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.news-medical.net/health/Shilajit-Health-Benefits-Risks-and-Clinical-Evidence.aspx', 'research library 2026-11 · F2 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Shilajit composition review; Stohs 2014', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'Shilajit may interact with diabetes, blood-pressure and hormone-related medicines.', 'Taking medication or managing a health condition? Check with your doctor before shilajit.', 'Taking medication or managing a health condition? Check with your doctor before shilajit.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.news-medical.net/health/Shilajit-Health-Benefits-Risks-and-Clinical-Evidence.aspx', 'research library 2026-11 · F4 · SS', 'shilajit', 'Shilajit clinical evidence review; Pandit 2016', 'ingredient', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'safety', 'As a precaution, shilajit is not for children, or during pregnancy or breastfeeding.', 'Not for children, or during pregnancy or breastfeeding.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.news-medical.net/health/Shilajit-Health-Benefits-Risks-and-Clinical-Evidence.aspx', 'research library 2026-11 · F5 · CO', 'shilajit', 'Precautionary guidance from shilajit review summaries', 'ingredient', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Caffeine works by blocking adenosine receptors, delaying the drowsiness adenosine builds up.', 'Caffeine doesn''t create energy. It blocks adenosine, the ''sleep pressure'' signal, for a while.', 'Caffeine doesn''t create energy. It blocks adenosine, the ''sleep pressure'' signal, for a while.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK430790/', 'research library 2026-11 · G1 · SS', 'both', 'StatPearls Caffeine (NBK430790); Jacobson, PMC9251831', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Caffeine''s average half-life is about 5 hours (1.5 to 9.5 hours depending on the person).', 'Half of an afternoon coffee''s caffeine can still be in your system about 5 hours later.', 'Half of an afternoon coffee''s caffeine can still be in your system about 5 hours later.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sites/books/NBK430790/', 'research library 2026-11 · G2 · SS', 'both', 'StatPearls; Jacobson', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'FDA cites 400 mg a day of caffeine as an amount not generally linked with negative effects in healthy adults, about two to three 12 oz cups of coffee.', 'FDA: about 400 mg of caffeine a day is the general upper amount for healthy adults.', 'FDA: about 400 mg of caffeine a day is the general upper amount for healthy adults.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://uthealthaustin.org/blog/spilling-the-beans-on-caffeine-health', 'research library 2026-11 · G3 · SS', 'both', 'FDA ''Spilling the Beans'' (2024); UTHealth Austin', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'An 8 oz coffee has about 80 to 100 mg caffeine, an 8 oz energy drink about 40 to 250 mg, tea 30 to 50 mg and soda 30 to 40 mg.', 'Energy drinks range from about 40 to 250 mg of caffeine per 8 oz. Check the label.', 'Energy drinks range from about 40 to 250 mg of caffeine per 8 oz. Check the label.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://extension.illinois.edu/blogs/simply-nutritious-quick-and-delicious/2021-06-14-how-much-caffeine-too-much', 'research library 2026-11 · G4 · SS', 'both', 'UTHealth Austin; Illinois Extension (citing FDA)', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Too much caffeine can cause restlessness, a fast heartbeat and poor sleep, and regular users can get withdrawal headaches.', 'Jitters, racing heart, 3 a.m. eyes open? Too much caffeine can do that.', 'Jitters, racing heart, 3 a.m. eyes open? Too much caffeine can do that.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://extension.illinois.edu/blogs/simply-nutritious-quick-and-delicious/2021-06-14-how-much-caffeine-too-much', 'research library 2026-11 · G6 · SS', 'both', 'Illinois Extension; Cleveland Clinic', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Drake 2013: 400 mg caffeine taken 6 hours before bed cut total sleep by 41 minutes, and participants were unaware of the disturbance.', 'Caffeine 6 hours before bed can still shorten sleep, often without you noticing.', 'Caffeine 6 hours before bed can still shorten sleep, often without you noticing.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2013/11/131114155838.htm', 'research library 2026-11 · G7 · SS', 'both', 'Drake et al., J Clin Sleep Med 2013;9:1195; AASM release', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'NCCIH: a growing body of evidence shows energy drinks can have serious health effects, particularly in children, teenagers and young adults.', 'NIH: energy drinks can carry real health risks, especially for teens and young adults.', 'NIH: energy drinks can carry real health risks, especially for teens and young adults.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://nccih.nih.gov/health/energy-drinks', 'research library 2026-11 · G8 · SS', 'both', 'NCCIH Energy Drinks', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Melatonin is a hormone the brain releases in the evening that signals sleep timing; it is not an adaptogen.', 'Melatonin is your body''s ''it''s night'' signal. Adaptogens like ashwagandha work differently, supporting your stress response over time.', 'Melatonin is your body''s ''it''s night'' signal. Adaptogens like ashwagandha work differently, supporting your stress response over time.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://health.ucdavis.edu/blog/cultivating-health/melatonin-and-your-sleep-is-it-safe-what-are-the-side-effects-and-how-does-it-work/2025/02', 'research library 2026-11 · G9 · SS', 'both', 'NCCIH Melatonin; UC Davis Health', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'US adult melatonin use rose from 0.4% (1999 to 2000) to 2.1% (2017 to 2018).', 'Melatonin use among US adults rose about fivefold over two decades.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://jamanetwork.com/journals/jama/fullarticle/2788539', 'research library 2026-11 · G10 · CO', 'both', 'Li et al., JAMA 2022;327:483', 'general', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Alcohol helps people fall asleep faster but disrupts the second half of the night and reduces REM sleep.', 'A nightcap may knock you out faster, but it fragments the second half of your night.', 'A nightcap may knock you out faster, but it fragments the second half of your night.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/acer.12006', 'research library 2026-11 · G11 · SS', 'both', 'Ebrahim et al., Alcohol Clin Exp Res 2013, PMID 23347102', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Owen 2008: 100 mg L-theanine with 50 mg caffeine improved attention-switching speed and accuracy vs caffeine alone or placebo.', 'L-theanine, an amino acid from tea, has been studied alongside caffeine for smoother focus.', null, 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/b95805cfcceb6637410e93b9fb4f7a41692751d1', 'research library 2026-11 · G12 · CO', 'both', 'Owen et al., Nutr Neurosci 2008, PMID 18681988', 'general', 'caption'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Ashwagandha and shilajit are not stimulants and contain no caffeine; their trials ran for 4 to 12+ weeks of daily use, while caffeine acts within an hour.', 'Coffee works in about 30 to 60 minutes. Ashwagandha root works with you over weeks: no caffeine, no jitters.', 'Coffee works in about 30 to 60 minutes. Ashwagandha root works with you over weeks: no caffeine, no jitters.', 'approved', true, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Ashwagandha-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · G13 · SS', 'both', 'NIH ODS; Cureus 2026; UTHealth Austin', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Adult magnesium RDAs range from 310 to 420 mg a day (about 400 to 420 for men, 310 to 320 for women).', 'Magnesium matters: adults need roughly 310 to 420 mg a day from food and drink.', 'Magnesium matters: adults need roughly 310 to 420 mg a day from food and drink.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://ods.od.nih.gov/factsheets/Magnesium-HealthProfessional/', 'research library 2026-11 · G15 · SS', 'both', 'NIH ODS Magnesium fact sheet', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'comparison', 'Caffeine''s effect peaks 30 to 60 minutes after intake and can linger 10 to 12 hours in some people.', 'That 3 p.m. latte can still be with you at bedtime.', 'That 3 p.m. latte can still be with you at bedtime.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://uthealthaustin.org/blog/spilling-the-beans-on-caffeine-health', 'research library 2026-11 · G16 · SS', 'both', 'UTHealth Austin; StatPearls', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Cortisol follows a daily rhythm with a sharp rise after waking, the cortisol awakening response.', 'Cortisol isn''t the villain. It naturally rises in the morning to help you get going.', 'Cortisol isn''t the villain. It naturally rises in the morning to help you get going.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18854200/', 'research library 2026-11 · H1 · SS', 'both', 'Fries et al., Int J Psychophysiol 2009, PMID 18854200', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'Cortisol rises by about 50% or more within 30 minutes of waking (Wüst 2000, 509 adults; Pruessner 1997).', 'Within 30 minutes of waking, cortisol rises by about half or more. That''s your built-in alarm.', 'Within 30 minutes of waking, cortisol rises by about half or more. That''s your built-in alarm.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/neuroscience/cortisol-awakening-response', 'research library 2026-11 · H2 · SS', 'both', 'Wüst et al. 2000; Pruessner et al., Life Sci 1997', 'general', 'any'),
('3034c840-dfc2-4c85-b949-bc8d4fd69208', null, 'fact', 'After its morning peak, cortisol declines across the day to its lowest point near bedtime.', 'Healthy rhythm: cortisol high in the morning, winding down by night.', 'Healthy rhythm: cortisol high in the morning, winding down by night.', 'approved', false, 'research', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/18854200/', 'research library 2026-11 · H3 · SS', 'both', 'Fries 2009', 'general', 'any'),
